course: dictionary
lesson: 11065
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Ask yourself: is someone measuring something, or are they thinking hard? «The bee hummingbird from Cuba weighs about two grams.» Here weigh means how heavy the bird is.
explain: Weigh can also mean to find out how heavy something is, using scales. «The bag weighs 5 pounds» tells you how heavy the bag is. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: "The bag is 5 pounds heavy" still makes sense.
explain: Weigh up is a phrase with a different meaning: to think carefully about choices before you decide. Nobody is using scales when they weigh up two options. Look for clue words like choices, options or decide to spot it.
fact: Weigh is a verb: weigh, weighs, weighed, weighing.
fact: To weigh something means to find how heavy it is, usually on scales or a balance.
fact: «The bee hummingbird from Cuba is the smallest bird in the world; it weighs about two grams.» Two grams is a very light weight.
fact: «All of them together still weigh less than all the people on Earth.» Here weigh is used to compare the weights of two groups.
fact: Weigh up means to think carefully about choices before you decide.
exercise: «The bee hummingbird weighs about two grams.» What does weighs mean here? | *To be that heavy | To think carefully before deciding | To hang down | To push water aside
exercise: Mia has to weigh up two schools before she chooses one. What does weigh up mean? | To be very tall | To carry a bag home | To find how heavy the schools are | *To think carefully about choices before deciding
exercise: The scales help us weigh the apples. What does weigh mean? | *To find how heavy something is | To sink under water | To be very light | To decide quickly
test: Which sentence uses weigh to mean think carefully? | The scales weigh the parcel | *She will weigh up her choices before she decides | The ship weighs ten tonnes | The bag weighs five pounds
test: What does weigh mean in «the bag weighs 5 pounds»? | *To be that heavy | To count the bags | To find how fast it moves | To cover in paint
exam: Which meaning of weigh is used in «Felix Gonzalez-Torres made a pile of sweets weighing the same as his partner»? | To think carefully before deciding | *To be that heavy, the same weight as his partner | To glow in the dark | To go up in a lift
